From f75f19b541d55d82f67ab3f9e64ced8c2be1bfbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: grenudi <idunerg@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:23:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-xiaomi-surya: capture through the TX
 SoundWire DAI

The TX SoundWire controller has one data-out and six data-in ports, so
its DAI 0 is a playback DAI: in the capture link it never gets
hw_params, the capture ports are never programmed, and every recording
through TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3 is digital silence although the stream runs.
Use the controller's DAI 1, as the sm8550/x1e boards with a WCD938x on
the same kind of controller do.

Found in pulpoff/linux-surya, which records surya's microphones this
way on mainline.

Tested on a Xiaomi POCO X3 NFC (surya).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
index 9424915df..8ccb810fd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-surya.dtsi
@@ -131,7 +131,7 @@ cpu {
 			};
 
 			codec {
-				sound-dai = <&wcd937x 1>, <&swr2 0>, <&txmacro 0>;
+				sound-dai = <&wcd937x 1>, <&swr2 1>, <&txmacro 0>;
 			};
 
 			platform {
